  "question_stem": "The velocity of a particle moving in a straight line is $v \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ at time $t$ seconds after leaving a fixed point $O$. The diagram shows a velocity-time graph which models the motion of the particle from $t = 0$ to $t = 16$. The graph consists of five straight line segments. The acceleration of the particle from $t = 0$ to $t = 3$ is $3 \\text{ m s}^{-2}$. The velocity of the particle at $t = 5$ is $7 \\text{ m s}^{-1}$ and it comes to instantaneous rest at $t = 8$. The particle then comes to rest again at $t = 16$. The minimum velocity of the particle is $V \\text{ m s}^{-1}$.\n{{figure:diagram_q05_01}}",
